(ENV-03, ENV-04: `first` and `last` are the full "NAME=value" string
 (LANGUAGE.md:4893-4894), so a non-empty entry contains an `=`. The entry
 is read into a text, copied into a buffer, and its bytes scanned for 61
 in one For each line - one line, because a loop split across lines would
 take a period from 'gen join lines' on its first line and close with an
 empty body. Loop-bearing, so top level only, like 'gen leaf while'. The
 entry is sometimes also read straight into a second buffer and the two
 sizes asserted to agree.)

To 'gen leaf environment entry scan' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    Set gen_envs to gen_envs add 1.
    a list called 'the lines' is [].
    a text called 'the row' is "ENV-03".
    a text called 'the source' is "environment's first".
    a number called 'the end draw' is 'rng below' of 13.
    If 'the end draw' is less than 6 then,
        Set 'the row' to "ENV-04",
        Set 'the source' to "environment's last".
    a text called 'the entry stem' is 'gen environment name'.
    a text called 'the entry' is 'gen buffer reference' of 'the entry stem'.
    a text called 'the scan' is 'gen environment companion' of "in bytes".
    a text called 'the scan size' is 'gen buffer property' of 'the scan' and "size".
    a text called 'the tally' is 'gen environment companion' of "equals signs".
    a text called 'the place' is 'gen environment loop word'.
    append "a text called {'the entry'} is {'the source'}" to 'the lines'.
    append "a buffer called {'the scan'} is {'the entry'}" to 'the lines'.
    append "a number called {'the tally'} is 0" to 'the lines'.
    append "For each {'the place'} from 1 to {'the scan size'}, If byte {'the place'} of {'the scan'} is 61 then, Set {'the tally'} to {'the tally'} add 1." to 'the lines'.
    a text called 'the tally shown' is 'gen buffer slot of' of 'the tally'.
    append "If {'the scan size'} is not 0 and {'the tally'} is 0 then, Print \"ASSERT {'the row'}: expected 1 got {'the tally shown'}\", Exit 95. Print {'the tally'} as a boolean" to 'the lines'.
    a number called 'the second reading draw' is 'rng below' of 13.
    If 'the second reading draw' is less than 7 then,
        a text called 'the direct stem' is 'gen environment name',
        a text called 'the direct' is 'gen buffer reference' of 'the direct stem',
        a text called 'the direct size' is 'gen buffer property' of 'the direct stem' and "size",
