(TIM-46 (LANGUAGE.md:4645-4649, undocumented): a timer that was never
 started reads 0 for every property and reports itself not running;
 `Stop` before any `Start` is not an error, but leaves `duration` reading
 the whole monotonic clock the timer measures with - the machine's
 uptime, not any interval this program asked for. The uptime number is
 machine- and boot-dependent, so only "absurdly larger than anything
 this program could have waited" is assertable; the floor below (60000
 ms, one minute) was comfortably clear of every uptime seen while
 hand-verifying this batch.)

