    a list called 'the tail lines' is ['the stop line', 'the running after check', 'the absurd floor check'].
    'gen join lines' of indent and nested and 'the tail lines'.

(TIM-47 (LANGUAGE.md:4625, undocumented): starting a timer that has
 already run RESTARTS it - the second `duration` measures only the
 second job, never the sum. The manual says nothing about a second
 Start; this is the shape that shows the reset rather than an
 accumulation. Waits are drawn far enough apart (500-699 ms vs 50-149 ms)
 that ordinary scheduler jitter cannot close the gap between them. The
 two stored readings are named through 'gen flow witness name' - both
 are asserted bare, with no property attached.)

