(TIM-51 (LANGUAGE.md:4606-4609, undocumented - the other half of
 Discrepancy 3): a negative duration in SECONDS returns at once - the
 kernel rejects a negative `tv_sec` outright. This is the safe half; the
 milliseconds half never returns at all (an unsigned divide turns a
 negative count into roughly 585 million years, D3.vox), which is why no
 leaf on this surface emits a millisecond `Wait`/`Sleep` with a negative
 operand and this one never will either - only the word
 `second`/`seconds` appears below, hand-verified on both compilers to
 return in well under the assertion's own 3-second ceiling.)

To 'gen timer negative wait line' with a number called 'the magnitude'.
    a number called 'the verb draw' is 'rng below' of 2.
    a number called 'the for draw' is 'rng below' of 2.
    a number called 'the plural draw' is 'rng below' of 2.
    a text called verb is "Wait".
    If 'the verb draw' is 1 then,
        Set verb to "Sleep".
    a text called 'the for word' is "".
    If 'the for draw' is 1 then,
        Set 'the for word' to "for ".
    a text called unit is "second".
    If 'the plural draw' is 1 then,
        Set unit to "seconds".
    a number called 'the negative magnitude' is 0 minus 'the magnitude'.
    a text called 'the line' is "{verb} {'the for word'}{'the negative magnitude'} {unit}".
    Return a text, 'the line'.

